summary: '[Jinx (advocate)] Ran the panel-mandated LLM-judge falsifier: 36 fully-blind Sonnet judges over all 18 ground-truthed Guard hits + 18 era/size-matched clean-merge controls. The kill condition ("judge matches 3/3 at tolerable false-flag rate") is decisively FALSIFIED — the judge caught zod 69ff844b exactly (doubled ${issue.minimum}) but MISSED the flagship zod 66cbfe09 ZodRecord defect while looking straight at the Partial<Record> diff, and missed xstate 7b808af4 (defect lines verifiably absent from the merge view). But the judge''s single control flag (0.88, highest of the run) was a REAL merge-created cross-branch interaction defect (xstate 72058a08: new test expecting old getDescription format x format change; same-day fix f6d20164c) in a merge the oracle classified CONVERGENT — the only such defect in the 275-merge corpus, caught by the LLM and structurally invisible to symbol-local knot detection.'
